{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1170845-sympathetic-connection-of-a-spell","id":1170845,"title":"Sympathetic Connection of a Spell","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-26T20:23:40-08:00","id":1170845,"title":"Sympathetic Connection of a Spell","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> So I have a question, can you use Correspondence on a spell to track down the person that cast it, because according to the description for the spell it seems perfectly possible:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Correspondence (Space \u2022)<br /> Practice: Knowing<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Academics, Empathy, Medicine<br /> We are all of us defined by our connections, and through this spell a mage learns those definitions. For every level of Potency, the mage learns one of the subject's sympathetic links. The spell reveals the subject's oldest and strongest links first. She understands these connections in the same manner the subject thinks of them (e.g. &quot;my childhood home,&quot; not &quot;1414 Willowbrook Drive, Columbus, OH&quot;). If the other half of the sympathetic link is within the mage's sensory range, she knows that and knows its exact location.<br /> +1 Reach: The mage can &quot;follow&quot; a trail of sympathetic links. When she learns of one of her initial subject's sympathetic connections, she may choose to learn one of that subject's connections, and so on. For example, she might follow a wedding ring to its owner, then its owner's spouse, then the spouse's place of employment.<br /> +1 Reach: The mage understands the emotional character of the connection in broad terms. &quot;My childhood home&quot; might carry notes of comfort and safety or fear and loathing, depending on the subject's upbringing.<br /> +2 Reach: The mage may specify the connections she wishes to uncover in general terms (&quot;an object with a strong link to his childhood&quot;) or (&quot;those she hates&quot;). Again, the knowledge is contextualized based on the subject's perceptions.<br /> +2 Reach: If the subject is a Keyed spell or Iris (p. 243), the mage may use one level of Potency to discover the Key instead of a link. </div> </div> </div>I ask because one of my players noticed a spell was cast in an area that they were investigating and decided to get the sympathetic connection to track down the mage that cast the spell initially. They didn't spend any extra reach to get a trail, but I did give them kind of a vague understanding of where the mage was when casting the spell.<br /> <br /> Or would the spell if analyzed reveal &quot;Creator&quot; and show an image of the person that cast the spell since it is based on how the subject &quot;thinks&quot; of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T22:54:27-08:00","id":1170868,"title":"","content":"Considering a mage has a medium connection to his own spells then yes its possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T02:49:24-08:00","id":1170888,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that Correspondence allows you to track something physically unless you're within sensory range. So you'd be able to identify the medium connection that likely leads to the Mage that cast it, but then would have to cast another spell using Sympathy to find out where they are if the Mage isn't in sensory range.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I'm right either though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-27-2017, 06:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T05:58:47-08:00","id":1170915,"title":"","content":"Eh, my take on sympathetic connections is that if you were able to isolate a specific connection that it points and stretches directly all the way to what it is connected to. Thus you could theoretically walk all the way from one end of the connection to the other. It'd be very interesting if that ISN'T how sympathetic connections work, like if they disappear or perhaps travel through the supernal realms or something.<br /> <br /> Granted, I would rule that you would have to keep the spell active for the duration of your journey or have to use Space mage sight the whole way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","user":"Falcon777","date":". 12-27-2017, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T07:48:40-08:00","id":1170945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1170845-sympathetic-connection-of-a-spell?p=1170888#post1170888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that Correspondence allows you to track something physically unless you're within sensory range. So you'd be able to identify the medium connection that likely leads to the Mage that cast it, but then would have to cast another spell using Sympathy to find out where they are if the Mage isn't in sensory range.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I'm right either though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeh i think the &quot;follow&quot; reach part confused me also, I read it as you can follow the link to the thing, but it actually reads like you just get that subjects subjects connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T07:58:31-08:00","id":1170947,"title":"","content":"You could still technically find the Mage using the follow reach option to find their place of employment. If they don\u2019t have that there is something else that will eventually lead you down to a specific spot. Unless there is something I am missing, unless you are a Mastigos or have an imbued item someone can track down any Mage that cast a spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T08:15:57-08:00","id":1170950,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s precisely what we're talking about. Note how the word follow is in quotations, in other words it\u2019s not a literal following but jumping from one set of Sympathetic Connections to another. Space spells dealing with Sympathy seem to generally target one or the other of a connection or a subject via its connection. Correspondence targets the former, whereas something like Locate Object can target the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T10:26:38-08:00","id":1170982,"title":"","content":"Btw, what if you follow the connection to a dead person? Do I tell the mage he sees a dead body or do I say that the connection he wants doesn't exist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T10:40:48-08:00","id":1170987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1170845-sympathetic-connection-of-a-spell?p=1170982#post1170982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw, what if you follow the connection to a dead person? Do I tell the mage he sees a dead body or do I say that the connection he wants doesn't exist?</div> </div> </div> </div>You only get a general sense of the nature of the connection, at best you also receive information of the emotional content of that connection. If the person that\u2019s your subject has Sympathetic connections to someone whose died then whether they know it, and how long the person has been dead will change the strength of the connection and the information that can be gleaned from it, but the connection would still be there until it naturally decays over time (or is altered by magic).<br /> <br /> So, say you cast on someone searching for their Sympathetic connection to their father. It\u2019s strong, and carries a loving emotional resonance. You Borrow the Threads, ask what dad\u2019s name was and open a Scrying window to the father. Turns out he\u2019s lying dead on his living room floor, looks like a heart attack that happened the night before.<br /> <br /> You release the borrowed thread and tell the kid the bad news, and then watch the connection\u2019s emotional content change to include grief. It\u2019s still there, but it will eventually fade as one half of the relationship is no longer there to maintain the connection.<br /> <br /> It could be argued that ghosts exist in part to make sure those connections never fade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T12:22:17-08:00","id":1171025,"title":"","content":"Interesting, just wanted to make sure I understood the spell correctly. I appreciate the help! Now it seems the players can find this Mage using Correspondence if they are clever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T17:38:27-08:00","id":1171110,"title":"","content":"How long do you think it would take a connection from a spell to deteriorate? Would 1 day after the spell ends reduce the connection by 1 level? I was curious about this in the event the characters stumble across a spell that was cast, but it has ended for all intents and purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T17:47:04-08:00","id":1171112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1170845-sympathetic-connection-of-a-spell?p=1171110#post1171110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long do you think it would take a connection from a spell to deteriorate? Would 1 day after the spell ends reduce the connection by 1 level? I was curious about this in the event the characters stumble across a spell that was cast, but it has ended for all intents and purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine it would be very quick, I have a hard time believing a Mage attaches a great deal of importance to most of his spells, especially the ones that were designed to end in short order. The only reason the connection is Medium in the first place is because of the metaphysical effort involved in putting a spell together and maintaining it with a portion of your spell control or WP. Basically, I think that connection could fade completely within a scene, certainly within 24 hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T18:16:11-08:00","id":1171117,"title":"","content":"As long as the spell is maintained I think it should stay on Medium. If it's cancelled or its duration runs out, well then the spell doesn't exist anymore and neither does any sympathetic connections that spell might've had.<br /> Sympathetic connections connect two things. If one of those things doesn't exist then there can't be a connection anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T19:53:52-08:00","id":1171138,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> I may be comparing apples and oranges here, so I apologize in advance. However, it appears that the signature nimbus persists for 1 week by default for mages under Gnosis 5 based on the book:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When she uses a spell, Praxis, Rote, or Attainment, she leaves little wisps of her identity on that magic. A mage utilizing Focused Mage Sight can recognize those signatures she\u2019s seen before. If the signature comes from a particularly great Gnosis (6+), it offers a bonus to Revelation rolls regarding that Pattern. For every dot of Gnosis above five, add one die to relevant dice pools. By default, this lasts for a week. </div> </div> </div>This seems to indicate that there is some connection between the mage and their spells even after they are cancelled/ended. Maybe I am reading too much into the signature nimbus and its relation to the mage itself and this may be only on active spells since the book is vague on whether this applies to spells that are no longer active. However, it does appear in the Sympathy Chart that items marked with a signature nimbus are considered medium connections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T01:20:37-08:00","id":1171170,"title":"","content":"That's different. The nimbus implies you still have a connection to the subject of the spell, at least until the nimbus disappears. But the subject of a spell and the spell itself are two different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T10:49:55-08:00","id":1171264,"title":"","content":"Thanks, that makes sense. Appreciate the assistance!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}